HYG v4.1 by David Nash / Astronexus, CC BY-SA 4.0.
https://github.com/astronexus/HYG-Database
Pinned source: c7f7f883fe678cc7680169a50ccd7dcc49b060ce
Derived data: 25 precise overlay stars and 99,049 background stars of magnitude
<=9.5, coordinate/unit conversion and compact storage. Derived numeric data retain
CC BY-SA 4.0, distinct from the app code license. See docs/data/star-catalog.md
and bundled HYG attribution/legalcode for full modification details.

Deep Star Maps 2020: NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center Scientific Visualization
Studio; Gaia DR2: ESA/Gaia/DPAC. https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4851/
Modified from linear RGB to sRGB JPEG; 16K source tiled into 4K/8K/16K levels with
pixel gutters and a 2K fallback; legacy 4K maps retained. Scientific coordinates
are preserved. Sources, hashes and conversions: docs/data/ and bundled sky/ATTRIBUTION.txt.
No NASA logo or endorsement is claimed. Imagery is separate from numerical positions.

The planning-page landscape is an OpenAI image_gen-generated decorative scene,
not an observation, location photograph or terrain model. Launcher and interface
vectors are project artwork, not Apple, Star Walk, Sky Map or NASA brand assets.

AndroidX/Compose, Kotlin, Coroutines, Okio and other resolved runtime artifacts:
versions, SHA256, original POM evidence and full license texts are retained in
android/app/src/main/assets/licenses/runtime-dependencies.json and docs/dependencies/.
Gradle lockfiles and verification metadata also preserve build/test inputs.
HSV-Alpha Color Picker source is retained with its Apache-2.0 LICENSE/NOTICE;
it is not an app runtime dependency.

Source and build scripts are provided in this repository. No signing keys are
included. Local debug builds use the developer's own Android debug certificate.
This preview has no completed outdoor AR angular-accuracy acceptance; phone
sensor/camera alignment is distinct from numerical astronomy calculations.
